  "lineage": "The formal Friday (jumuah) and Eid sermon delivered by the khatib from the minbar, a two-part homily of praise, Qur'anic citation, exhortation, and supplication codified from the earliest Medinan community. It is delivered in heightened, projected Arabic oratory that frequently cadences into maqam-inflected dua and quoted Qur'anic verse. The rhetorical structure — opening hamd and salawat, admonition, and closing prayer for the community — is preserved across the Sunni and Shia worlds. It stands alongside the adhan and tajwid recitation as a central genre of Islamic vocal practice, though speech-centered rather than fully melodic.",
